draw  maps.  I've  also  improved  the  program  that  uses  this  data,
gcdist(1), so it understands higher precision, among other things.

I posted the gcdist (great circle distances and headings) package a long
time (two  years?)  ago.  Rather than repost it here and now, since it's
about  25Kb of  source,  let me know by mail if you  would  like a copy.
I'll mail it to you, or, if I get enough  requests (or one from ARPAnet,
the great unreachable beyond :-) ), I'll post it after all.

Please, no flames about using net.sources; it seems like the right place
for this sort of thing, and it's at least as useful as some of the OTHER
stuff in this notesfile...

